    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0123" n="801" xml:id="pg801"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 420.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 24, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 2d instant, (No. 356,) communicating a copy of a note of the 1st
                    instant, addressed by you to Mr. Drouyn de l’Huys, relative to the proposed
                    manning of the Florida in a French port with a crew brought thither from a
                    British port. Your course in the matter is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
